        {
          "audience": "all",
          "basis": "",
          "command": "tensward analyse --project /p/lp --engine-arg max-num-seqs=16 --goal tpot",
          "costs": "trade-off: TTFT worsens (requests wait longer to be admitted); throughput falls as fewer sequences run in each step; requests queue if the load grows (TTFT up, throughput down)",
          "evidence": "strong",
          "key": "lower-concurrency",
          "kind": "suggestion",
          "name": "lower-concurrency",
          "near": false,
          "plan": [
            "then (prediction): queueing before scheduling likely binds next (watch for requests waiting at the lowered cap)"
          ],
          "quality_risk": false,
          "reason": "decode ran at 62% of the memory-bandwidth ceiling at the measured batch; with 32 sequences running at the cap, half as many per step read less KV cache each step, so each token comes sooner",
          "test": "about 6 min on this setup (this run: 64 s to load, 4.4 min to warm up and measure)",
          "tier": "try_first"
        },
        {
          "audience": "all",
          "basis": "your prompts",
          "command": "tensward analyse --project /p/lp --engine-arg 'speculative-config={\"method\": \"ngram\", \"num_speculative_tokens\": 4, \"prompt_lookup_max\": 4}' --goal tpot",
          "costs": "TPOT rises when answers do not copy the prompt, and at high concurrency; a slower start",
          "evidence": "moderate",
          "key": "ngram-speculation",
          "kind": "suggestion",
          "name": "ngram-speculation",
          "near": false,
          "quality_risk": false,
          "reason": "prompts are long (median 299 words beyond what they share). N-gram speculation drafts tokens by copying spans of the prompt, so it only helps when answers quote or repeat their input; otherwise it costs a little - compare TPOT with and without it",
          "test": "about 6 min on this setup (this run: 64 s to load, 4.4 min to warm up and measure)",
          "tier": "try_first"
        },
        {
          "audience": "all",
          "item": false,
          "key": "could_help",
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Could help:",
          "tone": "plain"
        },
        {
          "audience": "all",
          "basis": "",
          "command": "tensward analyse --project /p/lp --engine-arg gpu-memory-utilization=0.95 --goal tpot",
          "costs": "does not change TPOT (fewer preemptions, but more sequences in each step); helps throughput and TTFT; less memory headroom: the engine may fail to start",
          "evidence": "strong",
          "key": "more-kv-memory",
          "kind": "suggestion",
          "name": "more-kv-memory",
          "near": false,
          "quality_risk": false,
          "reason": "raising max_concurrent_requests above 32 is blocked: requests queue at the cap and the highest sampled KV-cache usage is 57%, too high for a larger cap to fit; kv_memory_fraction is the engine default. Raising it to 0.95 gives the engine more of the GPU's memory for the KV cache, which may not be enough to raise the cap, and leaves the GPU less memory headroom, so the engine may fail to start or run out of memory",
          "test": "about 6 min on this setup (this run: 64 s to load, 4.4 min to warm up and measure)",
          "tier": "could_help"
